 across multiple mocks."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/verifying-interactions","title":"Verify Every Interaction"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/mocking-your-first-protocol#Create-the-system-under-test":{"title":"Create the system under test","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In this tutorial you’ll test a "},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that depends on a "},{"code":"PricingService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — without writing a mock class by hand. You’ll mark a protocol with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Mockable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", let the macro generate the mock, stub what its method returns, and verify that your code actually called it."}],"role":"pseudoSymbol","kind":"section","type":"section","url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Create-the-system-under-test","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/mocking-your-first-protocol#Create-the-system-under-test"},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/Table-Of-Contents":{"url":"\/tutorials\/table-of-contents","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents","kind":"overview","type":"topic","title":"Meet SwiftMocking","role":"overview","abstract":[{"text":"Stop hand-writing mock classes. With SwiftMocking, one ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Mockable"},{"text":" annotation turns any protocol into a fully featured mock: stub return values, match arguments with expressive matchers, drive callbacks, and verify every interaction — all type-safe, all local, no code generation steps in your build.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftMocking/tutorials/SwiftMocking/dynamic-stubbing#Return-computed-values":{"url":"\/tutorials\/swiftmocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Return-computed-values","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftMocking\/tutorials\/SwiftMocking\/dynamic-stubbing#Return-computed-values","role":"pseudoSymbol","abstract":[{"text":"Fixed return values only go so far. Real d